{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Related Documentation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp"],"anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"generated":true,"title":"Explanation","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"],"anchor":"Explanation"}],"kind":"article","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/DesignPrinciples","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"text":"The 10 rules that shape every Swidux app, and the reasoning behind them.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swidux\/designprinciples"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swidux"}],"role":"article","title":"Design Principles","roleHeading":"Article"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux"],["doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux’s surface area looks small — a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol — but the API is opinionated. These principles explain "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"why","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the API has the shape it does, so you can extend it correctly."}]},{"text":"1. State is a value, observation is a class","type":"heading","anchor":"1-State-is-a-value-observation-is-a-class","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"State is a struct. Mutations go through "},{"code":"inout State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", which is predictable, snapshottable, and testable. SwiftUI observation needs an "},{"code":"@Observable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" reference type. Reconciling these two requires a class that mirrors the struct."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Swidux","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" generates that class for you (","type":"text"},{"code":"<StructName>Observer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") and wires up the ","type":"text"},{"code":"SwiduxObservable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance that bridges the two. Don’t hand-write the observer. The ","type":"text"},{"code":"pack → reduce → unpack-diff → observe","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" cycle is what gives you per-property re-renders without coupling reducers to a class.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"@Slice","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" extends this to nested struct slices: each slice gets its own observer class so observation stays granular even across composition.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"2. Reducers are pure and synchronous","type":"heading","anchor":"2-Reducers-are-pure-and-synchronous","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Reducers take "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inout State"},{"type":"text","text":" and an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Action"},{"type":"text","text":", mutate state in place, and return an optional "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect"},{"type":"text","text":". They never "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"type":"text","text":", never "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"throw"},{"type":"text","text":", and never call I\/O directly."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why: pure synchronous mutations are trivially testable, deterministic, and snapshot-friendly. When you need async work (network, disk, timers), return an effect — a ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" async closure that runs off the MainActor and dispatches follow-up actions back through ","type":"text"},{"code":"send","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"3-Effects-run-off-MainActor-sends-hop-back","type":"heading","text":"3. Effects run off MainActor; sends hop back"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@Sendable (Send) async -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The "},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" runs effects in "},{"code":"Task { @concurrent in }","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" so they don’t block UI. "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"code":"@MainActor @Sendable (Action) -> Void","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", so dispatching from inside an effect always lands back on MainActor — no manual hops, no race conditions on state."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is deliberate: effects own the work, the reducer owns the state."}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"4-Persistence-is-invisible","type":"heading","text":"4. Persistence is invisible"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Reducers mutate ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" properties; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" records every change in a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" debounces and drains those changesets through "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":" closures."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You never write "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" in a feature. A reducer that adds an item is identical whether the entity is persisted to SwiftData, SQLite, or nowhere — register or don’t register a writer. This is the principle that makes Swidux apps feel small: persistence stops being a concern of feature code."}]},{"text":"5. Synchronous state, async persistence","type":"heading","anchor":"5-Synchronous-state-async-persistence","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"State updates synchronously inside the reducer for instant UI feedback. Persistence happens asynchronously: ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","type":"reference"},{"text":" change tracking is in-memory and free; the debounced persistence flush coalesces rapid mutations into a single batched write.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tap-tap-tap-tap on an increment button updates the UI on every tap and produces one DB write a moment later. Reducers stay synchronous; storage stays cheap."}]},{"text":"6. Plugins are the single extension point","type":"heading","anchor":"6-Plugins-are-the-single-extension-point","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Everything that hangs off the dispatch cycle is a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Persistence, undo, killswitch, parental gate, paywall — same protocol, same lifecycle hooks. You can add your own without forking Swidux.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Two structural patterns:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Core middleware","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":") — action-agnostic. Doesn’t know your action type. Couples only to state shape (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":" for undo; "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" keypaths for persistence)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Domain plugins"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ParentalGatePlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallPlugin","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", your own) — owns a state slice and an action enum. Wires into your root types via keypath + action lifter + extractor.","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The decision rule: ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"does this need to know your action type?","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" If no, write core middleware and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"willReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"code":"afterReduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". If yes, write a domain plugin and use ","type":"text"},{"code":"reduce","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"anchor":"7-Bind-to-the-store-not-to-State","text":"7. Bind to the store, not to `@State`","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Form inputs read from the store and dispatch on write. Use "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)"},{"type":"text","text":" for the common case (read one property, dispatch one action), and fall back to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Binding(get:set:)"},{"type":"text","text":" when the read is a transformation (optional unwraps, derived values) or the setter wraps the dispatch in animation or branching. Don’t buffer mutable form state in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":" and write back on a button."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Why: every mutation flows through the reducer, which means undo\/redo, persistence, and any plugin that watches the dispatch cycle sees every keystroke (subject to coalescing). If you stash state in ","type":"text"},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", those plugins are blind to it.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The trade-off is more dispatches per keystroke. Coalescing — see "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" — collapses bursts of the same action into a single undo step."}]},{"text":"8. Registration order matters at the boundaries","type":"heading","anchor":"8-Registration-order-matters-at-the-boundaries","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" snapshots in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"willReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so it must run "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"before"}]},{"type":"text","text":" any plugin or reducer mutates state — register it first. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" drains changelogs in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"afterReduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so it wants the post-mutation state — register it after undo. Domain plugins use only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"reduce"},{"type":"text","text":", so their relative order rarely matters."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The recommended order:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["plugins.register(undoPlugin)         \/\/ 1. snapshots first","plugins.register(persistencePlugin)  \/\/ 2. drains after reducer","plugins.register(killswitchPlugin)   \/\/ 3. domain plugins","plugins.register(paywallPlugin)","plugins.register(parentalGatePlugin)"]},{"text":"9. Strict concurrency, on purpose","type":"heading","anchor":"9-Strict-concurrency-on-purpose","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux is built for ","type":"text"},{"code":"swiftLanguageMode(.v6)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and assumes Swift 6 strict concurrency throughout. State must be ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". The macros mark generated code carefully. Effects use explicit isolation (","type":"text"},{"code":"@Sendable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"@concurrent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is friction at first — you’ll get warnings about "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":" types. Honour them. The result is a state-management layer that composes safely with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async\/await"},{"type":"text","text":" and SwiftData without the surprise data races you get from pre-Swift 6 designs."}]},{"type":"heading","text":"10. The store is opinionated; your app is not","anchor":"10-The-store-is-opinionated-your-app-is-not","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swidux gives you a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Store","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a reducer protocol, a plugin protocol, and three optional plugins. It does not give you:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A dependency-injection container (write your own ","type":"text"},{"code":"AppEnvironment","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A navigation library (use SwiftUI navigation).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A network layer (use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"URLSession"},{"type":"text","text":", structured concurrency, or whatever you want)."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An opinion on database (SwiftData, GRDB, SQLite, Core Data — register a "},{"code":"StateWriter","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and Swidux doesn’t care)."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The store owns one job: take an action, produce a new state, run effects. Everything else is yours.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","text":"11. Service shapes: protocol when others implement it, closures when we own it","anchor":"11-Service-shapes-protocol-when-others-implement-it-closures-when-we-own-it","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Swidux services deliberately come in two shapes, chosen by who supplies the implementation:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — when apps or vendor adapters implement the backend:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"PaywallService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (RevenueCat, StoreKit, simulated), ","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(Mixpanel, Amplitude, console), ","type":"text"},{"code":"FeatureFlagsService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (any JSON host).","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A protocol gives conformers a stable, documented contract.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Struct of closures"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" — when the library owns the shape and apps only","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"configure or mock it: ","type":"text"},{"code":"KillswitchService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"ParentalChallengeSource","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"SyncPreflightService","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Closures make the built-in ","type":"text"},{"code":".live","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"\/","type":"text"},{"code":".mock","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"factories and per-test overrides trivial without a conformance ceremony.","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The split is a signal, not an accident: if you find yourself conforming to a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"struct-of-closures service, that service was designed to be configured, not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"replaced."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Anti-patterns","anchor":"Anti-patterns"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"await"},{"text":" or ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try"},{"text":" inside a reducer — return an effect instead.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Hand-writing the observer class when you could use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Swidux"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Calling "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"db.save()"},{"type":"text","text":" from inside a reducer — use "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Mutating state from inside an effect — effects dispatch actions; the reducer mutates."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ Owning the store with "},{"code":"@StateObject","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" — use "},{"code":"@State","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Store"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Observable"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ObservableObject"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Buffering form state in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"text":" and committing on submit — bind to the store directly.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"❌ Registering ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin"},{"text":" before ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin"},{"text":" — snapshot must precede mutation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ArchitectureGuide":{"title":"Architecture & Performance","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/architectureguide","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ArchitectureGuide","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the architectural patterns that make Swidux work correctly with SwiftUI’s observation system."}],"role":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/UndoPlugin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/UndoPlugin","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"UndoPlugin","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Snapshot-based undo\/redo plugin."}],"url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/undoplugin","title":"UndoPlugin"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SwiduxPlugin":{"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"SwiduxPlugin","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SwiduxPlugin","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/swiduxplugin","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A plugin that participates in the Swidux dispatch cycle."}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SwiduxPlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PersistencePlugin":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PersistencePlugin","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/persistenceplugin","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Coalescing persistence plugin."}],"title":"PersistencePlugin","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PersistencePlugin"}]},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/EntityStore":{"title":"EntityStore","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/entitystore","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/EntityStore","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"EntityStore"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"EntityStore","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An ordered, keyed collection of identifiable entities that silently records"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"every mutation for downstream persistence."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/SecurityPosture":{"title":"Security Posture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/securityposture","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/SecurityPosture","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What Swidux’s soft controls actually guarantee, and what to do when you need a hard one."}],"role":"collectionGroup"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Effect":{"title":"Effect","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/effect","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Effect","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Effect","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"An async unit of work returned by a reducer.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/ChangeSet":{"title":"ChangeSet","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/changeset","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/ChangeSet","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ChangeSet"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Tracks which entity IDs have been created\/updated or deleted."}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Store/binding(_:sending:)":{"title":"binding(_:sending:)","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/store\/binding(_:sending:)","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Store\/binding(_:sending:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"binding","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"KeyPath","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7KeyPathC"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"State","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Observer","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:6Swidux0A10ObservableP8ObserverQa"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sending","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Binding","preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI7BindingV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"Binding","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that reads a property through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"observer tree and dispatches an action when written.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","conformance":{"constraints":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"State"},{"type":"text","text":" conforms to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SwiduxObservable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"type":"text","text":"Conforms when"}]}},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/Send":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/Send","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Send","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/send","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A function for dispatching actions back to the store from within an effect."}],"title":"Send"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/PluginArchitecture":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/PluginArchitecture","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/pluginarchitecture","type":"topic","role":"article","title":"Plugin Architecture","abstract":[{"text":"Extend the dispatch cycle with lifecycle hooks — from invisible infrastructure to domain-specific features.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/BuildingYourFirstApp":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/BuildingYourFirstApp","role":"article","kind":"article","type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/buildingyourfirstapp","abstract":[{"text":"Build a counter app from scratch and meet the four moving parts of a Swidux project: state, action, reducer, and store.","type":"text"}],"title":"Build Your First Swidux App"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux","url":"\/documentation\/swidux","type":"topic","role":"collection","abstract":[{"text":"Redux-style state management for SwiftUI, with macros for observability and ready-made plugins for persistence, undo, paywalls, version killswitches, and parental gates.","type":"text"}],"title":"Swidux","kind":"symbol"},"doc://Swidux/documentation/Swidux/StateWriter":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Swidux\/documentation\/Swidux\/StateWriter","url":"\/documentation\/swidux\/statewriter","type":"topic","role":"symbol","title":"StateWriter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Accumulates entity snapshots and produces batched async persistence work."}],"kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StateWriter"}]}}}